Permission allow rule (../../../../.claude/settings.json): Bash(git -C * push origin claude/*) has a wildcard before the rest of the command, so it also matches any options inserted at that position and approves them without a prompt. For git, options such as -c and --exec-path can run arbitrary commands. Replace that * with the exact value you mean, or only use * after the subcommand (for example Bash(git status *)).
